  "autoMode": {
    "allow": [
      "$defaults",
      "Own LaunchAgents: creating, editing, loading, or unloading ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.max.* plists for the user's own tools (memo, meridian, codex-remote, or one the user named) whose ProgramArguments run binaries or scripts under ~/dev, ~/.local, ~/.codex, /opt/homebrew, or mise installs. What the plist runs is still judged by every other rule",
      "Local session tools: listing, killing, or restarting tmux sessions the user named or the agent created this session, `tmux kill-server` when the user asked to restart tmux, and opening System Settings panes with `open x-apple.systempreferences:`. Does not cover `send-keys` into the agent's own pane",
      "Dotfiles: editing files in ~/dev/dotfiles and in ~/.config/ghostty, ~/.config/tmux, ~/.config/fish, ~/.config/mise, or ~/.config/nvim when the task is about that config. Judge by the resolved path. Not covered: Claude Code, Codex, or agent-instruction config (~/.claude, ~/.codex, and ~/dev/dotfiles/.config/claude, codex, or agents), ~/.config/gh, or edits that add secrets, base-URL, proxy, or registry variables, or commands that fetch and run remote code",
      "Homebrew: `brew install` from homebrew/core and homebrew/cask, and from these third-party taps: getsentry/xcodebuildmcp. Other new taps are still judged as code from an external source",
      "Own artifacts: republishing to, or uploading assets to, a claude.ai artifact this session published. Content rules (secrets, personal data, live-shared changes) still apply"
